---
title: "Stocking a Small Pantry for Real Weeknights"
description: "The handful of staples that make weeknight cooking possible when the nearest store is 40 minutes away."
date: "2026-08-05"
author: "DevInTheMtn"
tags: ["essay", "pantry"]
---

When the nearest grocery store is a real drive, "just run out and grab it" stops being an option. What's worked for us is keeping a small, boring list of staples on hand at all times: canned tomatoes, dried beans, good olive oil, a couple of vinegars, alliums that keep, and a rotating stock of grains.

None of it is exciting on its own, but it means almost any recipe on this site can be pulled together from what's already in the cabinet, plus whatever's fresh that week. That's the actual goal of the pantry list — fewer trips, not a bigger one.
